        <IRI>http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/tove/census#CensusProfile</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A Census Profile is a profile that contains all of the published data found in a given census.

A Census Profile has the following properties:
•hasTime: Identifies the year of the census
•hasCharacteristic: Identifies the categories of data found in the Census Profile</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/tove/census#Characteristic</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A Characteristic is an indicator used to represent statistical data about a population or geographic location.

A Characteristic has the following properties:
•hasValue: Identifies the corresponding Measure instance that represents the value of the Characteristic
•cardinality_of: Identifies the Population instance that is described by the Characteristic, if applicable
•hasLocation: Identifies the geographic location for the Characteristic
•hasPart: Identifies the subcharacteristics associated with a given Characteristic</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
